 ## 8. The channel kind
 
-The VFO defaults to DN (V/D mode 2) at Narrow deviation. Its W/N selection
-controls deviation independently of the data type. Quick's DT (data type) tile
-cycles V/D-1, DN and VW (with full-rate voice in the build). This radio-wide
-VFO setting is held in RAM, along with the other live YSF parameters. Stored
-YSF channels use the data type and deviation from their own parameter block.
+The VFO defaults to DN (V/D mode 2). Quick's Mode tile offers one YSF entry;
+its DT tile cycles V/D-1, DN and VW (with full-rate voice in the build). DT
+selection also sets the deviation: V/D-1 and DN use Narrow (1350 Hz), VW
+uses Wide (2700 Hz). The channel raster remains 12.5 kHz. This radio-wide
+VFO setting is held in RAM; stored YSF channels keep their own parameter
+blocks. Legacy saved VFO deviation overrides are discarded on restore.
 
 The radio glue is written: `RADIO_MODE_YSF`, `CODEPLUG_KIND_YSF` (kind 6),
